# The example extension open-tasks (installed in the empty home by tests/drive.rs) keeps a count
# of open tasks in the status line, the whiteboard's too. The whiteboard runs in the menu's loop,
# so the extension is answered while a drawing is open: a task another program writes shows in
# the count at once, and so does one typed on a sticky, without leaving the drawing.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for ☐ 16 open tasks
keys w
wait-for whiteboards · type to filter · ⏎ open · Esc back
type venn
keys enter
wait-for whiteboard Volcano Venn
expect ☐ 16 open tasks
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n
wait-for ☐ 17 open tasks
expect whiteboard Volcano Venn
# A new card with a task on it: the canvas owner reads it, and the extension hears of it.
keys n
wait-for editing · type text · ⏎ new line · Esc done (saves)
type - [ ] Count the masks
keys esc
wait-for ☐ 18 open tasks
expect whiteboard Volcano Venn
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
expect ☐ 18 open tasks
keys q
exits 0
